  "modName": "Echos of Gaia (Beta)",
  "description": "Echos of Gaia adds screen reader support, field/world navigation, deliberate automatic walking, battle/menu speech and optional audio descriptions to Windows Steam Final Fantasy IX. Beta 0.1.9 repairs current-area NPC/exit presentation, distinguishes same-name zones, fixes opening alley/steeple/rooftop Story steps and the first Evil Forest rescue approach, and restores masked dialogue-choice speech. Native-filtered interaction points survive route planning, and Main Street short steps respect native arrival tolerance. Includes the accessible launcher, double-click installer and 608 narration recordings. Whole-game coverage remains partial; some scenery bindings, generic NPC labels, puzzles and timed minigames still need work. Complete opening/forest, physical-controller and audible screen-reader testing remain separate from automated/native checks.",
